body:
`set_current_screen` should handle checking if the value is different, so we shouldn't need to check `if (current_window->get_current_screen() != screen) {` here.

And this is never called with a negative index besides -1 as far as I can tell, so there is no need to get the current screen.

So this could be:

```suggestion
	if (p_screen < 0) {
		return;
	}
	Window *current_window = get_window();
	if (current_window) {
		current_window->set_current_screen(p_screen);
	}
```

